# Joint R62/R63 HOST operator envelope

This refreshes the qualified R61 operator with a new scope and frozen R63 RAM
payload binding. No device has been opened. All TEMPLATE/ARGV files are inert:
a fresh exact Root grant and independent review are required for each stage.
The current canonical lease remains closed; this envelope does not change it.

For each finite proposed batch, first capture selected249 using the first
validated live status to learn the actual physical keycounter and epoch. A
historical counter is not an admission. Lock every subsequent status to that
fresh counter/epoch and bind later grants to the fresh typed snapshot hash.
The capture can save a nonzero/configured state, but it never authorizes reboot.
The current ROM/return path requires freshly demonstrated losslessly rebootable
zero data and admitted RTC_SET=0 HOLD. Any nonzero data, changed image or configured
clock stops before a transition and requires a separate concrete Root decision.
Do not infer permission to reset, overwrite, or globally restore user data.

The five following supervised stages are resident-to-ROM, exact-UID ROM dual
Flash read/load/verify/execute, math-only CDC, ROM return/read, and typed resident
verification. No Flash programming, SD writes, RTC setters or global restore.
Two fresh2MiB Flash copies must match before execution; the after copy must match
them. A mismatch stops before RAM execution. UI/value/stack/program/IP/cwd/alarm/
settings are checked against fresh data; no UI exception is inferred. SET0 clock
is documented HOLD, with no claimed exact calendar trajectory and no setter.
No entire-SD backup is claimed. All own actors/FDs must close and be reaped.

Only the four pinned new batches are proposals. No old30R61 batches resume. Each
batch binds its exact case IDs, unique nonce, query/byte/time budgets and explicit
normal X return. Revocation/expiry is checked before each native operation and
buffered response. Failure never causes automatic X, reset, retry or recovery.
The worker's legacy R55 protocol/USB/file identifiers name the same qualified
transport, not the selected mathematical revision. Worker code is unchanged;
five literal metadata words bind the accepted R63 math image. Full primitive
checks are inherited through exact-code proof; fake HOST tests are not physical
device, backup, clock or cycle evidence.
